<h2 id="ha-ctrl-012-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Check the distribution’s direction, source labels, kW against kWh, period changes, and missing or partial inputs. Do not change any native quantity.
2. Inspect a gauge at its minimum, maximum, out of range and unavailable. Inspect a pie with a missing category. Do not invent a threshold or a whole.
3. Test reduced motion, keyboard access, cues that are not colour, and a real value alternative for each named card or engine version. Record limits you could not resolve.
4. Switch away from Civica and update an unsupported card. Native behaviour must stay intact. No Energy table, ONS label or adapter marker may be invented.

Record what was tested using [Native task accessibility and evidence](native-task-accessibility.html). A source review or a local example is not a live-device check.

<h2 id="ha-ctrl-012-sources">Sources</h2>

Reviewed on 11 November 2026. Current documentation may describe a newer frontend than the one installed, so check the controls you actually have.

